![An orange tent on a lakeshore below a broad snow peak and dark rock walls, Cordillera Huayhuash, Peru](/images/blog/trekking-the-huayhuash-alpine-circuit-in-peru/01-dsc03069.webp)

Trekking the Huayhuash Alpine Circuit is **_undoubtedly_** one of the best experiences anyone could ever be fortunate enough to have in the mountains. Earlier this month, I completed my second full alpine circuit of the Cordillera Huayhuash in a personal record time and with a new route variant. In September/October of 2025, my friend Trey and I carried everything on our backs for more than 70 kilometers, ascended over 4600 meters, and climbed up 7 passes in 6 days and 5 nights. We started the trek in Quartelhuain and ended in Llamac, following the majority of the original alpine circuit (we skipped the alpine route of the first day).

![Elevation profile of the Huayhuash Alpine Circuit, with camps marked along about 70 kilometers](/images/blog/trekking-the-huayhuash-alpine-circuit-in-peru/02-profile.webp "Terrain stats from my second time completing the Huayhuash Alpine Circuit.")

This is a basic guide and photographic journey from the two trips I have completed over the past two years. Think of this blog as an art gallery. Scroll through slowly and let the images take you there. For photographers, you can learn more about [how I selected the lens I carried](/blog/choosing-the-right-lenses-for-adventure-photography) in another one of my informative posts. Thank you and enjoy the journey!

